      "description": "Programme Adrian Sutton ‘Montana Peaks’ Dectet Charles Villiers Stanford Serenade in F Major Bohuslav Martinu Nonet H.374 Blaze Ensemble return for another engaging Lunchtime Recital. The group are a London based chamber ensemble, with performances range from works for small wind and string ensemble to chamber orchestra. In addition to performing staples from their ensemble repertoire, Blaze Ensemble has commissioned new works from the UK’s most established contemporary composers, and for this recital, will include a piece written especially for them by British composer, Adrian Sutton who lived in Blackheath.",
