      "dedupe_key": "lifem26-exhibition-only|2026-11-12|blackheath-halls",
      "description": "The annual exhibition in Blackheath Halls is a fabulous showcase of all things early music, and an important marketplace attracting attendees from around the UK and the world. Makers and exhibitors are at the very beating heart of the festival, contributing to the legacy of early music exhibitions in London spanning over half a century. Established brands come together with highly respected individual makers, publishers, early music organisations, and more to create a vibrant atmosphere in the Great Hall. The exhibition is a popular destination for professionals, students, and enthusiasts alike. This year, for the first time, entry to the exhibition is free to all. Why not upgrade your ticket to the Exhibition Plus pass ? This gives you access to the Makers’ Demonstrations, Performers’ Platforms, Early Music Young Ensemble Competition, and our range of talks, presentations, and fringe events.",
      "ends_at": null,
      "image_url": "https://www.blackheathhalls.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/Exhibition-16.9-Web.jpeg",
