  {
    "date_text": "Sat 9 Oct, 7.30pm",
    "event": {
      "address": "23 Lee Road, London SE3 9RQ",
      "all_day": false,
      "category": "music",
      "dedupe_key": "leveret|2027-10-09|blackheath-halls",
      "description": "You choose the tunes, Leveret play them! For this special 2026 all-requests tour, the acclaimed English folk trio are putting their entire back catalogue in the hands of the audience. As you arrive, simply write down your favourite Leveret tunes and drop them into the request box. Then, live on stage, the trio will draw out your choices and bring them to life in a unique performance shaped entirely by you. Featuring three of England’s finest folk musicians, Andy Cutting (melodeon), Sam Sweeney (fiddle) and Rob Harbron (English concertina), Leveret combine extraordinary musicianship with an instinctive musical connection. Their playing is rooted in the English folk tradition, but their inventive approach gives familiar tunes a life of their own. Renowned for their intuitive interplay and captivating live performances, the trio create music in the moment, with no fixed arrangements and no two performances ever quite the same. Their repertoire brings together rediscovered traditional melodies, original interpretations and new compositions. With multiple BBC Folk Award wins between them and collaborations spanning some of the biggest names in folk music, the group are celebrated for their exceptional skill and musical chemistry. Whether you’re a lifelong folk fan or simply love live music played with passion and spontaneity, don’t miss this chance to choose the music and be part of a truly special Leveret performance.",
      "ends_at": "2027-10-09T20:20:00Z",
